# NestJS / TypeScript Rules

## Tooling
- Package manager: **npm** (not pnpm/yarn). Lock file is `package-lock.json`.
- Run dev: `npm run dev` (NestJS watch mode).
- Tests: `npm test` (Jest, regex `*.spec.ts`).
- Lint: `npm run lint`.

## Module structure
- One folder per feature under `src/modules/<name>/`.
- Files: `<name>.module.ts`, `<name>.controller.ts`, `<name>.service.ts`, `dto/<verb>-<name>.dto.ts`.
- Generate scaffolds with `npx nest g resource modules/<name>` then trim the spec file.
- Shared services (LLM, embeddings, search, etc.) live in `src/services/` and are exposed via `services.module.ts`.

## Validation
- HTTP request DTOs use `class-validator` + `class-transformer`.
- LLM structured-output schemas use `Zod` via Vercel AI SDK.
- `ValidationPipe` is registered globally in `main.ts` with `{ whitelist: true, transform: true }`.
- Never trust raw `req.body`.

## Database
- Drizzle is the only ORM. Schema lives in `src/db/schema.ts` (single source of truth).
- pgvector columns: `vector('embedding', { dimensions: 384 })`.
- HNSW index on every vector column: `index('...').using('hnsw', t.embedding.op('vector_cosine_ops'))`.
- Migration generation: `npm run drizzle:generate`. Apply locally: `npm run drizzle:migrate` (runs `tsx src/db/migrate.ts`).
- Commit every generated migration file under `drizzle/migrations/`.
- Raw SQL only via `db.execute(sql\`...\`)` and only when Drizzle's typed API can't express it.

## LLM access
- Always via `LlmService` (in `src/services/llm.service.ts`). Never instantiate `createOpenAI` elsewhere.
- Model name from `process.env.LLM_MODEL` — never hard-code. The env reader is `getEnv()` in `src/config/env.ts`.
- Use `generateObject` with a Zod schema for any structured output. `generateText + JSON.parse` is forbidden.
- All public LlmService methods wrap their generation in `this.withFreeTierFallback(...)` for 429 backoff + free-model cascade.
- On exhaustion, callers catch `LlmExhaustedError` and degrade the cycle to "no fresh briefing" rather than crashing.

## Workers
- BullMQ via `@nestjs/bullmq`. One processor per job type in `src/workers/`.
- Cron via `@nestjs/schedule` `@Cron`/`@Interval`. No external Beat process.
- Long steps acquire a Postgres advisory lock per query: `SELECT pg_advisory_xact_lock(query_id)`.
- Jobs are idempotent: a duplicate run produces no extra side effect.

## Logging / errors
- `nestjs-pino` is the logger. No `console.log` in committed code.
- Throw typed errors (`LlmExhaustedError`, `NotFoundException`, etc.) — never plain strings.
- Sentry hooks wire later; for now use the structured logger.

## Tests
- Jest + supertest. Each module has `<name>.service.spec.ts` and a controller spec where logic warrants it.
- Test files live alongside source OR in `test/` for cross-module integration tests.
